  "title": "A Fallen Limb Finds Its Footing",
  "mood": "Enclosed woodland; pale branching wood above rust earth",
  "reason": "Compared a lowering fallen limb, an opening fern gate and roots weaving steps. The limb best joins the narrow earthy passage in image01 to the interlaced pale wood in image02; gate loses wood topology and weaving weakens grounded attachment. Replace separate block banks with one continuous eroded hollow. A thick asymmetrically forked limb descends into a root cradle; grouped fern fans and tangled background boughs enclose rather than decorate it. This is invented geometry, not recovery.",
